[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html:18[39m.

  - Native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so the on/off state is browser-managed and clicking the text
    toggles it too.
  - One CSS rule strikes through the label text when checked, which is the visible "done" signal.

  No JS, no build step, no persistence — the state lives in the DOM and resets on reload. Say the word if you want it to
  persist (localStorage) or to render a list of items from data.

  I didn't run anything; it's a static page with no test setup in the repo.

